My name is Marco.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:11,170
And my name is Katrin and today we have an elementary level lesson for you guys out there.

4
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:11,970
That's right.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:16,430
Today we are going to talk about an interesting topic, especially for women.

6
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,490
We are going to the nail salon.

7
00:00:19,090 --> 00:00:22,570
Okay, so we're going to get our fingernails painted.

8
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:29,960
Alright, so let's take a look at vocabulary preview to find out what nail salon means.

9
00:00:29,960 --> 00:00:30,850
Vocabulary preview.

10
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:37,990
Alright so if you go to a nail salon, it's a specific place where they paint your nails, right?

11
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,080
Exactly.

12
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:42,790
So it's a shop or a store where you can have your nails painted.

13
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,730
So they have special people to help you.

14
00:00:44,990 --> 00:00:48,750
If you want to go get your hair cut, you would go to the hair salon.

15
00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:49,450
Exactly.

16
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:53,040
So we have hair salon and nail salon.

17
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:55,550
In this case, at the nail salon, they can't cut your hair.

18
00:00:56,040 --> 00:00:57,070
Okay, very good.

19
00:00:57,320 --> 00:01:00,750
So why don't we listen to our dialogue for the first time.

20
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,180
Honey, I'll be right back.

21
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:09,740
Where are you going?

22
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:10,960
I told you already.

23
00:01:11,320 --> 00:01:12,820
I'm going to get my nails done.

24
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:13,440
Again?

25
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,340
You just went last week.

26
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,720
You spend more time at the nail salon than you do here at home.

27
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:21,640
Honestly, why do you need a manicure every week?

28
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:25,720
Well, first of all, I like to pamper myself and my nails look great.

29
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:27,000
You should come with me.

30
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:27,600
Why?

31
00:01:28,250 --> 00:01:30,850
I don't want to have nail polish or anything like that.

32
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:32,670
They don't only paint my nails.

33
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:38,240
The manicurist will remove my cuticles, file my nails and apply at least four coats of nail polish.

34
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:41,190
Yeah, sounds like something I should definitely do.

35
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:47,880
All right, we're back.

36
00:01:47,880 --> 00:01:53,020
So now we found some very interesting and specific words related to nails.

37
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:56,380
So why don't we look at those now on Language Takeaway.

38
00:01:57,610 --> 00:01:58,830
Language Takeaway.

39
00:01:59,730 --> 00:02:05,830
All right, so this first word is an important word for every woman to know and I know a lot of men who get this too.

40
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,080
It's called a manicure.

41
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:08,490
All right, manicure.

42
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:11,150
And what exactly is a manicure?

43
00:02:11,410 --> 00:02:14,590
Well, a manicure is a service that you get at a nail salon.

44
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:21,510
And that means that the people at the nail salon will cut your nails and shape your nails.

45
00:02:21,730 --> 00:02:28,290
That means if you want them to be pointy or boxy and then you get them painted and dried.

46
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:33,760
Okay, so they basically take care of your nails, of your fingernails, a manicure.

47
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:34,180
Exactly.

48
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:37,840
And so the important thing to remember here that a manicure is for your hands.

49
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,880
Right, so you can also get your toenails or your feet taken care of, right?

50
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:42,340
Exactly.

51
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:43,700
So that's different.

52
00:02:43,980 --> 00:02:46,840
That's a pedicure because peda means foot.

53
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:50,980
So pedicure is for your feet and a manicure is for your hands.

54
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:52,200
All right, very good.

55
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:58,680
And well, we talked about painting your nails and that paint has a specific name, right?

56
00:02:59,360 --> 00:02:59,620
Exactly.

57
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:04,760
So you wouldn't use wall paint on your fingers, would you?

58
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:08,000
So you have to use a special paint and this is called nail polish.

59
00:03:08,680 --> 00:03:09,960
Nail polish, okay.

60
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:15,080
So a polish is something that makes a surface or a thing shiny.

61
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:19,280
Okay, so nail polish is a paint that makes your nails very shiny.

62
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:20,200
All right, very good.

63
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:29,760
And well, moving on, we talked about a manicure and there's a specific word for the person that provides this service that takes care of your nails.

64
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:33,580
Okay, so the job at a nail salon is manicurist.

65
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:37,080
That's the person who paints your nails, okay?

66
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:40,630
And so you could say, I have a favorite manicurist.

67
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,930
Her name is Sally.

68
00:03:42,410 --> 00:03:43,670
Okay, very good.

69
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:55,450
And well, a manicurist, they perform a manicure and well, apart from painting your nails, they also push your cuticles or remove your cuticles like in the dialogue.

70
00:03:55,970 --> 00:03:57,150
What are the cuticles?

71
00:03:57,610 --> 00:03:59,290
Okay, cuticle is a very hard word.

72
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:04,430
This word describes the skin around your fingernail, okay?

73
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:09,750
So you have skin all over your body, but on your fingernail, you have special kind of skin.

74
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:18,640
And so a manicurist will sometimes push or cut the dead skin, that's the cuticle, from your finger.

75
00:04:18,640 --> 00:04:19,310
Okay, very good.

76
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:26,560
And if you look at your fingernails now, you will see a little thin layer of skin on your fingernail.

77
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,550
That's the cuticle.

78
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:35,000
And well, apart from removing your cuticles and painting your nails, they will also file your nails.

79
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,380
And this is a verb, to file.

80
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:38,100
To file, okay.

81
00:04:38,360 --> 00:04:45,240
So this is a word that's kind of like cut or trim, but a file is a more delicate process.

82
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:50,580
So it means that we kind of shave off very, very, very little at a time.

83
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:58,720
And so to file your nails means to make them shaped differently or to smooth them.

84
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,480
They're not cutting, clip, clip, clip.

85
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,480
It's not that.

86
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,720
It's a little bit less than that.

87
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,800
And now there's also a noun for this, a nail file.

88
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:09,840
And most women will usually have it.

89
00:05:09,840 --> 00:05:15,880
It's a long piece of cardboard that has a paper that's kind of like sand on it, kind of like sandpaper.

90
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,640
It doesn't feel good when you rub it with your hand.

91
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:23,280
But if you use it on your nails, it will little by little just take away little parts of your nail.

92
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:25,240
Yeah.

93
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:25,970
Like that.

94
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:31,850
You usually see it, the many secretaries, you know, in TV shows, they're always filing their nails.

95
00:05:32,010 --> 00:05:32,270
Exactly.

96
00:05:33,440 --> 00:05:34,440
Making them perfect.

97
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,440
Okay.

98
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,040
So those are the words we have for language takeaway.

99
00:05:37,050 --> 00:05:41,110
Why don't we take a look at our dialogue again and we'll be back in a little bit.

100
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,420
Honey, I'll be right back.

101
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,300
Where are you going?

102
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:50,500
I told you already.

103
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,360
I'm going to get my nails done.

104
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:53,160
Again?

105
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,100
You just went last week.

106
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,480
You spend more time at the nail salon than you do here at home.

107
00:05:59,080 --> 00:06:01,420
Honestly, why do you need a manicure every week?

108
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:05,460
Well, first of all, I like to pamper myself and my nails look great.

109
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:06,760
You should come with me.

110
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:07,480
Why?

111
00:06:08,110 --> 00:06:10,750
I don't want to have nail polish or anything like that.

112
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:12,670
They don't only paint my nails.

113
00:06:13,120 --> 00:06:18,200
The manicurist will remove my cuticles, file my nails and apply at least four coats of nail polish.

114
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:18,610
Yeah.

115
00:06:19,200 --> 00:06:22,400
It sounds like something I should definitely do.

116
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:26,120
All right, we're back.

117
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:34,720
So now why don't we start with some phrases, some very good phrases that we found in this dialogue in Fluency Builder.

118
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:35,030
Fluency Builder.

119
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:42,600
This first phrase is really important when we talk about nails because it's the way that we describe going to the nail salon.

120
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:46,560
So I can say, I'm going to get my nails done today.

121
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:49,040
Okay, so to get your nails done.

122
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:54,840
That means that you're going to get your nails cut, filed, painted, etc.

123
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:57,840
I'm going to get a manicure, but that's very, I don't know, serious.

124
00:06:58,280 --> 00:07:00,040
So you could say, I'm going to get my nails done.

125
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:00,980
It's more spoken language.

126
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:05,240
Okay, so I'm going to get my nails done or you got your nails done.

127
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:06,320
Very good.

128
00:07:07,080 --> 00:07:13,040
And well, the woman was talking about why she likes to go get a manicure and she said that she likes to pamper herself.

129
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:22,300
Okay, this is very common, especially when women are trying to talk about why they spend money on hair and nails and clothes.

130
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:24,800
They say, I like to pamper myself.

131
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:27,400
To pamper means to treat very, very well.

132
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:27,630
Okay.

133
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:32,650
So if you go get a manicure, it's kind of like pampering yourself or maybe going to a spa.

134
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:34,490
Exactly, or getting a massage.

135
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:38,320
And so we could say also, don't pamper the dog.

136
00:07:38,320 --> 00:07:38,950
He's very naughty.

137
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,830
So a synonym would be to spoil.

138
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:44,510
To spoil oneself, to pamper.

139
00:07:44,930 --> 00:07:45,370
Indulge.

140
00:07:45,490 --> 00:07:45,810
Okay.

141
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:55,280
So, and well, she was talking about how they perform a manicure and she talked about four coats of nail polish.

142
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,090
So a coat, we know that it's kind of like a jacket, right?

143
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:00,510
But in this case, it means a layer.

144
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,910
So you paint your nails one time.

145
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:04,520
Okay.

146
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:04,850
You have color.

147
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,350
Maybe it doesn't look right.

148
00:08:06,870 --> 00:08:06,990
Okay.

149
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:07,650
It's very thin.

150
00:08:08,290 --> 00:08:16,950
So you say, okay, I'm going to paint two coats and then you paint one more time and the color gets darker and you paint one more time and the color gets very dark and very thick.

151
00:08:17,430 --> 00:08:18,390
And so these are called coats.

152
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,560
That means layers of nail polish.

153
00:08:20,730 --> 00:08:23,730
And that's a special word we use when we're talking about painting our nails.

154
00:08:24,150 --> 00:08:24,310
Right.

155
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:29,130
So not only for nails, but if you're painting your house, maybe you need two or three coats of paint.

156
00:08:29,530 --> 00:08:29,770
Exactly.

157
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:37,180
If we have a red wall and we want to paint it white, we definitely need two, three, maybe four coats of paint.

158
00:08:37,440 --> 00:08:38,740
Otherwise, we'll still see the red.

159
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:40,200
Okay.

160
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,200
Very good.

161
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,400
Very interesting phrases.

